# In insert mode (IRM) with autowrap (DECAWM) on, a character printed at
# the last column takes that column, and the character that stood there
# is lost. The cursor waits at the column with a pending wrap. The next
# character starts the next row and is inserted there, moving that row's
# text right.
# spec: the VT510 manual, IRM: "If IRM mode is set, then new characters move characters in page memory to the right. Characters moved past the page's right border are lost"; DECAWM: "If the DECAWM function is set, then graphic characters received when the cursor is at the right border of the page appear at the beginning of the next line"
# covers: ANSI-4
size 6 3
send "abcdef\e[2;1Hghij\e[1;6H\e[4hX"
dump
send "Y"
dump
